<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Chain Rule Application for Computing a Derivative</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the following functions,</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle w= {@func_w@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  x={@func_x@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  y={@func_y@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle z={@func_z@}\)</p>
<p>Use Chain Rule to compute \(\displaystyle \frac{dw}{dt}\). </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{dw}{dt} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<br>
<p>From this information it looks like the chain rule for this case should be, </p>
<p style="margin-left: 30px">\( \displaystyle
\frac{dw}{dt}= \displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{x}}\frac{d{x}}{d{t}}+\frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{d{y}}{d{t}}+\frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}\frac{d{z}}{d{t}} \) </p>
<p style="margin-left: 30px">\( \displaystyle \qquad= \displaystyle {@func1a@}({@func1b@})+{@func2a@}({@func2b@})+{@func3a@}({@func3b@}) \)</p>             
<p style="margin-left: 30px">\( \qquad= \displaystyle {@ta@}\)  </p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2023060500</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>/*Question variables*/
aa:rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
bb:rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
cc:rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
dd:rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);

func_w:expand((aa*x-z)*(x+bb*z))/y^(cc);
func_x:t^(dd)+cc;
func_y:cos(bb*t);
func_z:dd*t;

/*Worked solution*/
func1a:diff(func_w,x);  func1b:diff(func_x,t);
func2a:diff(func_w,y);  func2b:diff(func_y,t);
func3a:diff(func_w,z);  func3b:diff(func_z,t);
ta1:func1a*func1b+func2a*func2b+func3a*func3b;
ta:ratsimp(ta1);</text>
    </questionvariables>
