<p id="description">This STACK question asks students to apply the Chain Rule to compute the derivative \(\frac{dw}{dt}\) of a function \(w\) expressed in terms of variables \(x\), \(y\), and \(z\). Students are required to differentiate each component function with respect to the independent variable \(t\) and apply the Chain Rule appropriately to obtain the final result.</p>]]></text>
